 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Crackers, cheese, apple slices, banana nuts, that sort thing. Keep the milk and bread at home for now. That gives you time to stop at a little shop if you run out. Enter the forest at each end if you can, it discourages people from woods for days. A bar of chocolate or a bag of crisps is fine, keep it in your bag and only indulge at midday when you can buy food while you' still on open ground. If you expecting to stop and enjoy the views, bring a small one with sandwiches or crackers and cheese. If you' just getting on with hiking, leave it at home.",
